  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 109 AM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nRain/storm chances...Widespread rain/thunder expected today and\ntonight, continuing into Saturday. Recent model trends are a bit\nfurther north with the low and expected precipitation, with a\ncorresponding rise in precipitation chances (60-80%). Despite the\narea in a Marginal Risk for excessive rainfall, probabilistic data\nindicates the chance for exceeding an inch of rain today and\ntonight is rather minimal. The best chances are across the far\nsouthern CWA with a 20-40% chance of exceeding this threshold.\nTherefore, excessive rainfall is not expected to be a high impact. \nConvective activity should remain minimal due to weak shear (< 20 \nknots) and limited forcing. Overall, signs point toward a period \nof light to moderate stratiform rain today and tonight. \n\nExpect light rain to persist through Saturday morning as the cold\nfront continues to sag south. Dry weather should then settle in\nthrough the early part of next week as high pressure and upper\nlevel ridging build in across the region. A low pressure system\napproaching from the west will bring a return to the active\npattern in the middle part of next week with a chance (30-50%) of\nshowers and thunderstorms. The forcing and instability look rather\nweek during this period; therefore, high impact weather is not\nanticipated.\n\nSmoke... Expect air quality readings in the moderate (yellow)\ncategory today as an elevated smoke plume reaches the surface at\ntimes. Per upstream obs, little to no deterioration in visibility\nare expected.",
